text:
maya.chen: quick heads-up — I'm going to apply a small rollout tweak to the inference-cache StatefulSet and rotate the secret path in TF later today. want a quick +1 or any blocking concerns. the goals: reduce steady-state replicas to 2, stagger startup to avoid NFS thundering, and wire the new k8s secret path so pods pick up new creds without rolling everything at once.

josh: can you paste the exact k8s/terraform changes you'll run? want to sanity-check the partitioning and probe timing. :eyes:

maya.chen: yup. plan is to patch the sts to use partitioned rolling update with partition=1 (so we only restart 1 pod at a time) and add a startupProbe for the cache warmup. sample patch:

```
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: StatefulSet
metadata:
  name: inference-cache
spec:
  replicas: 2
  updateStrategy:
    type: RollingUpdate
    rollingUpdate:
      partition: 1
  template:
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: cache
        resources:
          requests:
            cpu: "250m"
            memory: "512Mi"
          limits:
            cpu: "500m"
            memory: "1Gi"
        startupProbe:
          exec:
            command: ["/bin/sh", "-c", "test -f /cache/ready || exit 1"]
          failureThreshold: 10
          periodSeconds: 10
        readinessProbe:
          httpGet:
            path: /health
            port: 8080
          initialDelaySeconds: 5
          periodSeconds: 10
```

maya.chen: terraform side — rotating secret involves creating kubernetes_secret with the new path and updating the deployment var. will use a lifecycle ignore_changes for annotation to avoid full recreate until we patch pods explicitly: 

```
resource "kubernetes_secret" "inference_cache_creds_v2" {
  metadata {
    name = "inference-cache-creds-v2"
    namespace = "prod"
  }
  data = {
    creds = filebase64("secrets/inference-cache/creds_v2.json")
  }
}

resource "kubernetes_stateful_set" "inference_cache" {
  # ... other fields ...
  spec {
    template {
      metadata {
        annotations = {
          "redwood.com/creds-version" = "v2"
        }
      }
      spec {
        container {
          env {
            name = "CACHE_CREDS_SECRET"
            valueFrom { secretKeyRef { name = kubernetes_secret.inference_cache_creds_v2.metadata[0].name key = "creds" } }
          }
        }
      }
    }
    # avoid TF recreates on non-critical annotations
    lifecycle {
      ignore_changes = [spec[0].template[0].metadata[0].annotations]
    }
  }
}
```

laura: I like partition=1, but make sure startupProbe covers the NFS mount timing — sometimes mounts take 40-60s. failureThreshold 10 @ period 10 => 100s which should be safe. also, bump readiness initialDelay to 20 for first pod.

ben: question — when you switch secret names we'll end up with both secrets present. whoever consumes the new secret via env var will still trigger a pod restart, right? how are you planning the migration to avoid double churn?

maya.chen: good Q. plan: create kubernetes_secret v2 first (no pod change). then update statefulset annotation to creds-version=v2 (we do this via kubectl patch to the template metadata) — because of lifecycle ignore_changes, TF won't immediately alter pods. then do a controlled rollout by bumping the partition or performing `kubectl rollout restart sts/inference-cache --namespace prod --patch='{"spec":{"template":{"metadata":{"annotations":{"redwood.com/rollout-ts":"<ts>"}}}}}'` one ordinal at a time (we'll `kubectl scale` to 3 temporarily if we need extra headroom).

josh: sanity check — do we need to temporarily increase replicas to avoid capacity blips during restart? if warmup is slow, scaling to 3 then partitioning down makes sense. also confirm HPA isn't fighting us (we have HPA on cache?).

maya.chen: there's no HPA on this sts. small cache, can bump to 3 for 5-10 mins during controlled rollout. I'll run load test locally then schedule the rollout for 1700 UTC.

deploy-bot: auto-check: infra-plan for branch "cache/creds-rotation" completed with 0 diffs to prod secrets path and 1 change (new kubernetes_secret resource). CI: unit tests passed. :white_check_mark:

laura: one more nit — add a postStart hook to touch /cache/ready when mounts are present to speed readiness for new pods. otherwise traffic still hits warm pods.

maya.chen: noted. I'll add a tiny postStart script and leave logs. ping me if you want to be on the call at rollout time. thanks for the quick reviews :thumbsup:
